    "q-103381": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103381",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $1≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\n\nII. $-5≡26\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$\n\nIII. $-1≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true because $8∣(1-9).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(1-9)÷8=-8÷8=-1\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false because $7∤(-5-26).$ Notice that $-5-26=-31,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- Statement III is false because $4∤(-1-4).$ Notice that $-1-4=-5,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
