    "q-212517": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212517",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the following congruence.\n\n$$\n-5≡\\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{A}}\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)\n$$\n\nWhich of the following values gives a true statement when inserted into the blank space?\n\nI. $-16$\n\nII. $7$\n\nIII. $17$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each case in turn.\n\n- Case I gives a true statement. Indeed, $11∣(-5-(-16)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-5-(-16))÷11=11÷11=1\n$$\n\n- Case II gives a false statement because $11∤(-5-7).$ Notice that $-5-7=-12,$ which is not divisible by $11.$\n\n- Case III gives a true statement. Indeed, $11∣(-5-17).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-5-17)÷11=-22÷11=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$-16$ and $17$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
