    "q-212509": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212509",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the following congruence.\n\n$$\n-7≡\\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{A}}\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\n$$\n\nWhich of the following values gives a true statement when inserted into the blank space?\n\nI. $-13$\n\nII. $2$\n\nIII. $11$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each case in turn.\n\n- Case I gives a true statement. Indeed, $3∣(-7-(-13)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-(-13))÷3=6÷3=2\n$$\n\n- Case II gives a true statement. Indeed, $3∣(-7-2).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-2)÷3=-9÷3=3\n$$\n\n- Case III gives a true statement. Indeed, $3∣(-7-11).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-11)÷3=-18÷3=-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$-13,\\,2,$ and $11.$\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
