    "q-76966": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76966",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given that $23≡-9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nI. $n=8$\n\nII. $n=4$\n\nIII. $n=2$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we remember that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=23-(-9)=32.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $8∣32$ because $32÷8=4,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $4∣32$ because $32÷4=8,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=4.$\n\n- Note that $2∣32$ because $32÷2=16,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
