    "q-212520": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212520",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given that $-20≡-6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$, which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nI. $n=2$\n\nII. $n=4$\n\nIII. $n=7$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-20-(-6)=-14.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣(-14)$ because $(-14)÷2=-7,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $4∤(-14).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=4.$\n\n- Note that $7∣(-12)$ because $(-12)÷7=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-212520-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-212520-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II only",
              "html": "II only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-212520-c",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "html": "I and II only"
            },
            {
              "option": "d",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-212520-d",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "html": "I only"
